@ref TA version table: Revised Edition 2000 (src:TA1999.20001230:226-227); Act 10 of 2005 published (src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:10-10); its commencement notification S 76/2005 (src:TA1999.S76-2005:3-3; src:TA1999.S76-2005:23-25); Act 19 of 2011 published (src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:9-9); S 33/2012 published and commencement (src:TA1999.S33-2012:3-3; src:TA1999.S33-2012:23-24); Act 15 of 2017 published, numbered, commencement clause and section 53(6) (src:TA1999.ACT15-2017:12-12; src:TA1999.ACT15-2017:22-22; src:TA1999.ACT15-2017:39-41; src:TA1999.ACT15-2017:4153-4154; src:TA1999.ACT15-2017:4217-4219); Legislative History entry 7 (src:TA1999:7181-7182; src:TA1999:7190-7190)
GIVEN `conduct day` IS A DATE
      `reading day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `Act text version`
`TA versions: the version of the Act's text that governs the conduct day, as read on the reading day` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 2 10 2026)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 2 10 2026)) THEN JUST `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 16 5 2018)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 16 5 2018)) THEN JUST `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 23 5 2017)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 23 5 2017)) THEN JUST `as amended by Act 15 of 2017`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 13 1 2017)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 2 2017)) THEN JUST `as amended by Act 30 of 2016`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 29 9 2016)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 10 2016)) THEN JUST `as amended by Act 22 of 2016`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 31 1 2012)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 1 2 2012)) THEN JUST `as amended by Act 19 of 2011`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 16 2 2005)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 16 2 2005)) THEN JUST `as amended by Act 10 of 2005`
           IF (`reading day` AT LEAST (Date 30 12 2000)) AND (`conduct day` AT LEAST (Date 30 12 2000)) THEN JUST `Revised Edition 2000`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Is the Act's own text, as enacted or printed, deposited for the version?  (The row after Act 15 of 2017 is not; Act 15 of 2017's own text is.)
GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`TA versions: the text of the version is deposited` MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `Revised Edition 2000` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 10 of 2005` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 19 of 2011` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 22 of 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 30 of 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 15 of 2017` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO` THEN TRUE

§ `What differs between the versions`

-- s 2 "equipment" in the Revised Edition 2000 and, unchanged, after Act 10 of 2005: "... used or intended to be used for telecommunication purposes".
-- Act 19 of 2011 section 2(b) replaced "telecommunication purposes" by "telecommunications, including (for the avoidance of doubt) any such
-- appliance, apparatus or accessory capable of being used for the operation of any broadcasting service" (1 Feb 2012).  The Bill's explanatory
-- statement says the clause is "to clarify that the term includes" equipment that is also capable of being used for broadcasting.
-- src:TA1999.20001230:226 | ‘‘equipment’’ includes any appliance, apparatus or accessory
-- src:TA1999.20001230:227 | used or intended to be used for telecommunication purposes;
-- src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:49 | (b) by deleting the words “telecommunication purposes” in the
-- src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:50 | definition of “equipment” and substituting the words
-- src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:51 | “telecommunications, including (for the avoidance of
-- src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:52 | doubt) any such appliance, apparatus or accessory capable
-- src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:53 | of being used for the operation of any broadcasting
-- src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:54 | service”;
-- src:TA1999.BILL20-2011:2571 | Clause 2(b) amends the definition of “equipment” in section 2 to clarify that
-- src:TA1999.BILL20-2011:2572 | the term includes any appliance, apparatus or accessory used or intended to be
-- src:TA1999.BILL20-2011:2573 | used for telecommunications which is also capable of being used for the
-- src:TA1999.BILL20-2011:2574 | operation of any broadcasting service.
@ref s 2 "equipment" (src:TA1999.20001230:226-227); Act 19 of 2011 section 2(b) (src:TA1999.ACT19-2011:49-54); Bill 20/2011 explanatory statement on clause 2(b) (src:TA1999.BILL20-2011:2571-2574)
GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`TA versions: s 2 "equipment" ends "used or intended to be used for telecommunication purposes"` MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `Revised Edition 2000` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 10 of 2005` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 19 of 2011` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 22 of 2016` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 30 of 2016` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 15 of 2017` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO` THEN FALSE

-- General penalties: s 65 of the 2000 Edition (s 85 today): a fine up to $10,000 or imprisonment up to 3 years or both, with forfeiture of any article seized.
-- Act 10 of 2005 section 28 added, after "or to both", "and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or part
-- thereof during which the offence continues after conviction".
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1916 | 65. Any person guilty of an offence under this Act or any
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1917 | regulations made thereunder for which no penalty is expressly
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1918 | provided shall, in addition to the forfeiture of any article seized, be
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1919 | liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprison-
-- src:TA1999.20001230:1920 | ment for a term not exceeding 3 years or to both.
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:961 | 28. Section 65 of the Telecommunications Act is amended by inserting,
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:962 | immediately after the words “or to both”, the words “and, in the case of a
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:963 | continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $1,000 for every day or
-- src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:964 | part thereof during which the offence continues after conviction”.
@ref s 65 of the 2000 Edition (src:TA1999.20001230:1916-1920); Act 10 of 2005 section 28 (src:TA1999.ACT10-2005:961-964)
GIVEN v IS AN `Act text version`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`TA versions: the general penalty has a further daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `Revised Edition 2000` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 10 of 2005` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 19 of 2011` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 22 of 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 30 of 2016` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Act 15 of 2017` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `as amended by Acts after Act 15 of 2017 that are not deposited` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the 2020 Revised Edition as deposited from SSO` THEN TRUE

-- Excluded matters: s 72 of the 2000 Edition (s 95 today).  Before Act 10 of 2005 it named the Singapore Broadcasting Authority Act (Cap. 297); after, the Broadcasting Act (Cap. 28).
-- Act 10 of 2005 also inserted in s 2 the definitions of "broadcasting apparatus" and "broadcasting service" by reference to the Broadcasting Act.
-- src:TA1999.20001230:2030 | 72. This Act shall not apply to the licensing of any broadcasting
